								<div class="title" id="post-title-4494125">
																		AUTHOR POST COFFER TOAST
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238055" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1581222426 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Feb 2020 04:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4494125">
									

<p>So here is very important research information I read yes: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osiris_myth">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osiris_myth</a></p>
<p>Also, image source is here: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Phallus_(hieroglyph">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Phallus_(hieroglyph</a>) Yes, this exists. Yes, you can see this in real life. Wild.</p>
<p>Big, big thanks to all of our chat reviewers! You are much appreciated and loved.</p>
<p>Thank you for Snappy in chat for providing the name for the article. Cheers!</p>
<p>I had a great time writing this&#8212;can't thank my co-author <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lvdoomien" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1593312); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1593312&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1581222426" alt="lvdoomien" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1593312)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lvdoomien" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1593312); return false;">lvdoomien</a></span> enough for being patient with my crazy schedule and meeting up to discuss and work on the draft over the last couple months. This has been in progress since December! lvdoomien had a lot of great ideas for the addenda content in particular, and I really enjoyed the back-and-forth regarding the wacky niche Ancient Egyptian mythology stories we discussed.</p>
<p>This is a sort of different feel on a standard SCP article. I was hoping we could convey just absolute flabbergast-ment on the part of the researchers who had to handle this anomaly, and crazy things happening faster than they could clinically record them. Because when the Sons of Horus are vandalizing your parking lot and birds are pooping all over your communication tower, who has time to write a perfectly clinical SCP document?</p>
<p>To all readers, I hope you enjoyed this!</p>

